WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.500
Two walkers.

2
00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:07.070
One city at night: rain, a
bridge, a stranger in a doorway.

3
00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:11.040
The first writer: The
streets went on and on.

4
00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:13.390
A figure watched from a doorway.

5
00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:16.220
The second: The streets shone.

6
00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:18.760
A stranger waved from a doorway.

7
00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:22.480
Neither writer says I
love it, or I fear it.

8
00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:25.840
So how do you spot an
attitude that nobody states?

9
00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:30.110
In this mission, you'll pull apart
three words that often get muddled:

10
00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:33.050
viewpoint, attitude and tone.

11
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.050
You'll go hunting for the
places where attitude hides,

12
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.610
clue by clue.

13
00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:41.190
And you'll walk the same streets
at night with two writers,

14
00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:44.120
one in 1860 and one today.

15
00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:47.660
Your mission: work out
how to spot attitude.
